## Why This Is Asked

Tests distributed systems correctness under concurrency, idempotency, ordering, and partial outages; validates that the API and ledger service maintain exactly-once semantics and message ordering.

## Key Concepts

- Idempotency keys, exactly-once processing
- Ordering guarantees in distributed ledger
- Partial upstream outages and retry semantics
- End-to-end testing with simulated upstream services and timeouts
- Tooling: Postman/Newman, k6, WireMock, Kafka test doubles

## Code Example

```javascript
// Example k6 test that repeats a payment request with same idempotency key
import http from 'k6/http';
import { check, sleep } from 'k6';

export default function () {
  const payload = { amount: 1000, currency: 'USD', account: 'A1' };
  const headers = { 'Content-Type': 'application/json', 'Idempotency-Key': 'abc-123' };
  const res = http.post('https://api/payments', JSON.stringify(payload), { headers });
  check(res, { 'status 200': (r) => r.status === 200 || r.status === 409 });

  sleep(0.5);
}
```

Note: The code snippet is minimal; ensure you adapt to your API.

## Why This Is Asked

This question probes an advanced testing scenario where data consistency is eventual and involves a read-model updated by a streaming pipeline, requiring tests around read-your-writes, consistency window, multi-tenant isolation, and resilience to streaming outages.

## Key Concepts

- Eventual consistency between read-model and stream
- Read-your-writes and drift windows
- Per-tenant isolation under concurrency
- Streaming fault injection and recovery
- Contract testing across gateway and downstream services

## Code Example

```javascript
// Example test sketch: verify eventual consistency
async function testReadYourWrites(tenantId, value){
  await writeMetric(tenantId, value);
  await untilTrue(async ()=> {
     const v = await readMetrics(tenantId);
     return v.includes(value);
  }, 30000);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you measure the real-world consistency window, and what metrics would you collect?
- How would you design roll-out and rollback strategies if drift exceeds SLA?
